<title>SWEDEN: KLM Cargo to start Skavsta-Amsterdam route.</title>
<headline>KLM Cargo to start Skavsta-Amsterdam route.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>KLM Cargo said on Wednesday it would start at least five flights a week from Sweden's Skavsta airport in Nykoping to its European hub at Amsterdam's Schiphol starting from February 17.</p>
<p>&quot;KLM Cargo has decided to move its flown cargo operations from Stockholm Arlanda airport to Nykoping Skavsta airport from February 17,&quot; KLM Cargo said in a statement.</p>
</text>
